      "key": {
        "uuid": "412d6321_79581596",
        "filename": "compos/composd_cmd/composd_cmd.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 145,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-22T17:17:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done\n\nNot specifically to this case, but I was worried that the compiler might optimize to drop earlier. But I can\u0027t find any reference (apparently there\u0027s no Rust specification).  Since all references say the drop happens at the end of the scope, I\u0027m gonna assume it\u0027s always the case.",
      "parentUuid": "3372ca29_15d7d874",
      "revId": "419029a3ed18c146c0cc03d4e6d7ca38691d88e4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5da0cdcf_d42f344c",
        "filename": "compos/composd_cmd/composd_cmd.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 145,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-22T17:25:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I dug into this once, and that is definitely true.\nThe lifetime may end earlier (at the last use of the variable - see \"non-lexical lifetimes), which allows the borrow checker to accept valid code that it otherwise wouldn\u0027t, but the actual drop occurs at the end of the scope.",
      "parentUuid": "412d6321_79581596",
      "revId": "419029a3ed18c146c0cc03d4e6d7ca38691d88e4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "02d3f990_c7c9abdb",
        "filename": "compos/composd_cmd/composd_cmd.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 145,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-22T17:27:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But it definitely can\u0027t drop it earlier than the previous line that uses it, right?",
      "parentUuid": "412d6321_79581596",
      "revId": "419029a3ed18c146c0cc03d4e6d7ca38691d88e4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a49084fa_f398c86e",
        "filename": "compos/composd_cmd/composd_cmd.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 145,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-22T17:34:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"may end earlier\" -\u003e it\u0027s our choice to make it end earlier?  If we do nothing, could we safely assume the compiler to drop it only at the end of the scope?",
      "parentUuid": "5da0cdcf_d42f344c",
      "revId": "419029a3ed18c146c0cc03d4e6d7ca38691d88e4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9d6d7751_f7b87873",
        "filename": "compos/composd_cmd/composd_cmd.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 145,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-22T18:01:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Andrew: Yes. But in fact the drop order here is well-defined and happens at the end of the scope, regardless.\nVictor: \"End of lifetime\" and \"point at which it gets dropped\" are not the same (I know this makes no sense, but that\u0027s the way it is). Both are determined by the compiler, but roughly the lifetime ends at the last reference and the drop occurs at the end of the scope.\nSo it is safe to assume it happens at the end of the scope.",
      "parentUuid": "a49084fa_f398c86e",
      "revId": "419029a3ed18c146c0cc03d4e6d7ca38691d88e4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
